   reader.onload = function(event) {
       const text = event.target.result;
       // Parse CSV here
       const data = parseCSV(text);
       displayCSV(data);
   };

   reader.onerror = function() {
       alert("Unable to read " + file.fileName);
   };

   reader.readAsText(file);
   ```

   - **Creating a FileReader:** `new FileReader()` creates a new FileReader object.
   - **onload Event:** This function runs when the file is successfully read.
     - `event.target.result` contains the file content as a string.
     - We call `parseCSV(text)` to parse the CSV data.
     - Then, `displayCSV(data)` displays the parsed data on the page.
   - **onerror Event:** Handles any errors during the file reading.
   - **readAsText:** Starts reading the file as plain text.

